.TH NUMDIFF 1
.SH NAME
numdiff \- compare outputs within tolerances
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B numdiff
[
.B \-t
.IB label =rel: x
|
.IB label =abs: x
] ...
.I expected actual
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Numdiff
compares two files line by line and field by field.
Words must be equal; numbers must agree within the tolerance of their
label (the last word before the number on its line), relative
.RB ( rel )
or absolute
.RB ( abs ),
or exactly if no tolerance is given.
Each mismatch is printed on one line.
.SH SEE ALSO
measure(1), cmp(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status 1 on a mismatch.
